hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17089","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Artah - meaning Ibn al-Mundhir - narrated to us, Damrah ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Nufayl al-Sakuni narrated to us, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when one said to him: O Messenger of Allah, were you brought food from heaven? He said: Yes. He said: And with what? He said: With a heated dish. They said: Was there excess in it beyond you? He said: Yes. He said: So what was done with it? He said: It was raised up, while it is revealed to me that I am withheld, not remaining among you, and you will not remain after me except a little. Rather you will remain until you say: When? And you will come in separate troops, some of you annihilating others. And before the Hour there will be severe pestilence, and after it years of earthquakes."
"17090","al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Sulayman, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that Salamah ibn Nufayl informed them that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have grown weary of horses, and I have laid down arms, and war has laid down its burdens. I said: There is no fighting. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Now fighting has come. There will always remain a group of my ummah manifest over the people; Allah will turn the hearts of peoples, and they will fight them, and Allah will provide them from them, until the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes while they are upon that. Verily, the settled abode of the believers is al-Sham, and horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
